IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`

-- Interpretation Act 1965 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from
-- 5 December 2025 -- LAYER 1, PART 2: GENERAL PROVISIONS REGARDING WRITTEN LAW, ss 3 to 18.
-- (s 10, the time a written law comes into operation, is in sgia-interpretation-time.l4.)
-- Each rule is a function over the yes/no facts it operates on. Where the Act says "unless the contrary
-- intention appears" (or "unless the context otherwise requires"), the function takes that as a plain
-- yes/no input and answers NOTHING when it is TRUE: the Act's default then no longer decides and the Act
-- does not say what does (NOTES.md finding 2).

§ `Section 3 -- Acts to be public Acts`

-- src:788 | 3. Every Act is a public Act, and is to be judicially noticed as such
-- src:789 | unless the contrary is expressly provided by the Act.
@ref s 3 (src:788-789)
GIVEN `the Act expressly provides that it is not a public Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an Act is judicially noticed as a public Act` `the Act expressly provides that it is not a public Act` MEANS
    NOT `the Act expressly provides that it is not a public Act`

§ `Section 4 -- Acts to be divided into sections without introductory words`

-- src:793 | 4. All Acts are to be divided into sections, if there be more
-- src:794 | enactments than one, which sections are deemed to be substantive
-- src:795 | enactments without any introductory words.
@ref s 4 (src:793-795)
GIVEN `the number of enactments in the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an Act must be divided into sections` `the number of enactments in the Act` MEANS
    `the number of enactments in the Act` GREATER THAN 1

@ref s 4 the sections are deemed substantive enactments without introductory words (src:794-795)
GIVEN `the section has introductory words` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a section is a substantive enactment` `the section has introductory words` MEANS
    -- deemed to be one "without any introductory words", whether or not it has any
    TRUE

§ `Section 5 -- Schedules`

-- src:799 | 5. Every Schedule to an Act, together with any note thereto, is to be
-- src:800 | construed and has effect as part of the Act.
@ref s 5 (src:799-800)
GIVEN `it is a Schedule to an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a note to a Schedule to an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is part of the Act and has effect as part of it` `it is a Schedule to an Act` `it is a note to a Schedule to an Act` MEANS
    `it is a Schedule to an Act` OR `it is a note to a Schedule to an Act`

§ `Section 6 -- Subdivisions of Acts`

-- src:804 | 6. When an Act is divided into Parts, Chapters, titles or other
-- src:805 | subdivisions, the fact and particulars of the division are, with or
-- src:806 | without express mention thereof in the Act, to be taken notice of in all
-- src:807 | courts and for all purposes.
@ref s 6 (src:804-807)
GIVEN `the Act is divided into Parts, Chapters, titles or other subdivisions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act expressly mentions the division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the division of an Act is taken notice of in all courts and for all purposes` `the Act is divided into Parts, Chapters, titles or other subdivisions` `the Act expressly mentions the division` MEANS
    IF `the Act is divided into Parts, Chapters, titles or other subdivisions`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- with or without express mention: the second input does not change the answer
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 7 -- Forms`

-- src:811 | 7. Except as is otherwise expressly provided, whenever forms are
-- src:812 | prescribed, slight deviations therefrom, not affecting the substance or
-- src:813 | calculated to mislead, do not invalidate them.
@ref s 7 (src:811-813)
GIVEN `forms are prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is otherwise expressly provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deviation is slight` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deviation affects the substance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deviation is calculated to mislead` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a deviation from a prescribed form invalidates it` `forms are prescribed` `it is otherwise expressly provided` `the deviation is slight` `the deviation affects the substance` `the deviation is calculated to mislead` MEANS
    IF `forms are prescribed`
       AND (NOT `it is otherwise expressly provided`)
       AND `the deviation is slight`
       AND (NOT `the deviation affects the substance`)
       AND (NOT `the deviation is calculated to mislead`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 7A -- Examples and illustrations`

-- src:817 | 7A. Where an Act includes an example or illustration of the
-- src:818 | operation of a provision —
-- src:820 | (a) the example or illustration is not to be taken as exhaustive;
-- src:821 | and
@ref s 7A(a) (src:817-821)
GIVEN `the Act includes an example or illustration of the operation of a provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the example or illustration is exhaustive` `the Act includes an example or illustration of the operation of a provision` MEANS
    IF `the Act includes an example or illustration of the operation of a provision` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Which prevails` IS ONE OF
    `the provision prevails`

-- src:817 | 7A. Where an Act includes an example or illustration of the
-- src:823 | (b) if the example or illustration is inconsistent with the
-- src:824 | provision, the provision prevails.
@ref s 7A(b) (src:817-824)
GIVEN `the Act includes an example or illustration of the operation of a provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the example or illustration is inconsistent with the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Which prevails`
`which prevails when an example is inconsistent with the provision` `the Act includes an example or illustration of the operation of a provision` `the example or illustration is inconsistent with the provision` MEANS
    IF `the Act includes an example or illustration of the operation of a provision` AND `the example or illustration is inconsistent with the provision`
    THEN JUST `the provision prevails`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 8 -- Mode of referring to written laws`

DECLARE `Way of referring to a written law` IS ONE OF
    `the year of its enactment and its number among the Acts enacted in that year`
    `its short title`
    `its chapter number and the year of the revised edition`
    `the citation the subsidiary legislation provides for`

-- src:831 | 8.—(1) It is sufficient for all purposes to refer to a written law —
-- src:833 | (a) in the case of an Act —
-- src:835 | (i) by the year of its enactment and its number among
-- src:836 | the Acts enacted in that year;
-- src:838 | (ii) where the Act, as enacted or revised, provides that it
-- src:839 | may be cited by a short title — by that short title; and
-- src:841 | (iii) where the Act is a revised edition published before
-- src:842 | 1 March 2021 under any law providing for a revised
-- src:843 | edition — by its chapter number and the year of the
-- src:844 | revised edition; and
-- src:846 | (b) in the case of a piece of subsidiary legislation that, as made
-- src:847 | or revised, provides for the manner of its citation — by that
-- src:848 | citation.
-- src:850 | [4/2021]
@ref s 8(1) (src:831-850)
GIVEN `the way` IS A `Way of referring to a written law`
      `it is an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act, as enacted or revised, provides that it may be cited by a short title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a revised edition published before 1 March 2021 under a law providing for a revised edition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsidiary legislation, as made or revised, provides for the manner of its citation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`it is sufficient for all purposes to refer to the written law in this way` `the way` `it is an Act` `the Act, as enacted or revised, provides that it may be cited by a short title` `it is a revised edition published before 1 March 2021 under a law providing for a revised edition` `the subsidiary legislation, as made or revised, provides for the manner of its citation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the way`
    WHEN `the year of its enactment and its number among the Acts enacted in that year` THEN
        IF `it is an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `its short title` THEN
        IF `it is an Act` AND `the Act, as enacted or revised, provides that it may be cited by a short title` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `its chapter number and the year of the revised edition` THEN
        IF `it is an Act` AND `it is a revised edition published before 1 March 2021 under a law providing for a revised edition` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `the citation the subsidiary legislation provides for` THEN
        IF (NOT `it is an Act`) AND `the subsidiary legislation, as made or revised, provides for the manner of its citation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:852 | (2) A reference for the purposes of subsection (1) may be made
-- src:853 | according to copies of written laws purporting to be printed or
-- src:854 | published by the Government Printer.
@ref s 8(2) (src:852-854)
GIVEN `the copy purports to be printed or published by the Government Printer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a reference may be made according to a copy of a written law` `the copy purports to be printed or published by the Government Printer` MEANS
    `the copy purports to be printed or published by the Government Printer`

-- src:860 | (3) Unless the contrary intention appears, a reference to a written
-- src:861 | law in accordance with subsection (1) is to be read as a reference to
-- src:862 | the written law as amended from time to time by any other written
-- src:863 | law.
@ref s 8(3) (src:860-863)
GIVEN `the reference is made in accordance with section 8(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the reference is read as a reference to the written law as amended from time to time` `the reference is made in accordance with section 8(1)` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `the reference is made in accordance with section 8(1)` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:867 | (4) Where —
-- src:869 | (a) a written law is referred to by its short title or citation,
-- src:870 | whether in any other written law or in any document; and
-- src:872 | (b) the short title or citation is subsequently changed,
-- src:874 | the reference is to be read, unless the contrary intention appears, as a
-- src:875 | reference to the changed short title or citation.
@ref s 8(4) (src:867-875)
GIVEN `the law is referred to by its short title or citation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the short title or citation is subsequently changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the reference is read as a reference to the changed short title or citation` `the law is referred to by its short title or citation` `the short title or citation is subsequently changed` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `the law is referred to by its short title or citation` AND `the short title or citation is subsequently changed` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 9 -- Construction in an Act of references to sections, etc.`

DECLARE `What a bare reference is to` IS ONE OF
    `a section, Part, Chapter or Schedule`
    `a subsection, paragraph or sub-paragraph`

DECLARE `Where a bare reference points` IS ONE OF
    `the Act in which the reference occurs`
    `the section in which the reference occurs`

-- src:884 | 9.—(1) Where in any Act there is a reference to a section, Part,
-- src:885 | Chapter or Schedule by number or letter only, and not in conjunction
-- src:886 | with the title or number of an Act, the reference is to be construed as a
-- src:887 | reference to the section, Part, Chapter or Schedule of that number or
-- src:888 | letter contained in the Act in which the reference occurs.
-- src:890 | (2) Where in any section of an Act there is a reference to a
-- src:891 | subsection, paragraph or sub‑paragraph by number or letter only, the
-- src:892 | reference is to be construed as a reference to the subsection,
-- src:893 | paragraph or sub‑paragraph of that number or letter contained in
-- src:894 | the section in which the reference occurs.
@ref s 9(1), (2) (src:884-894)
GIVEN `the reference is to` IS A `What a bare reference is to`
      `the reference is by number or letter only` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Where a bare reference points`
`where a reference by number or letter only points` `the reference is to` `the reference is by number or letter only` MEANS
    IF `the reference is by number or letter only`
    THEN CONSIDER `the reference is to`
         WHEN `a section, Part, Chapter or Schedule` THEN JUST `the Act in which the reference occurs`
         WHEN `a subsection, paragraph or sub-paragraph` THEN JUST `the section in which the reference occurs`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:896 | (3) This section applies, with suitable modification, to subsidiary
-- src:897 | legislation.
@ref s 9(3) (src:896-897)
GIVEN `it is subsidiary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 9 applies, with suitable modification` `it is subsidiary legislation` MEANS
    `it is subsidiary legislation`

§ `Section 9A -- Purposive interpretation of written law and use of extrinsic materials`

DECLARE `Which interpretation` IS ONE OF
    `the first interpretation`
    `the second interpretation`

-- src:902 | 9A.—(1) In the interpretation of a provision of a written law, an
-- src:903 | interpretation that would promote the purpose or object underlying
-- src:904 | the written law (whether that purpose or object is expressly stated in
-- src:905 | the written law or not) is to be preferred to an interpretation that
-- src:906 | would not promote that purpose or object.
@ref s 9A(1) (src:902-906)
GIVEN `the first interpretation would promote the purpose or object underlying the written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second interpretation would promote the purpose or object underlying the written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Which interpretation`
`the interpretation to be preferred` `the first interpretation would promote the purpose or object underlying the written law` `the second interpretation would promote the purpose or object underlying the written law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the first interpretation would promote the purpose or object underlying the written law` AND (NOT `the second interpretation would promote the purpose or object underlying the written law`) THEN JUST `the first interpretation`
        IF `the second interpretation would promote the purpose or object underlying the written law` AND (NOT `the first interpretation would promote the purpose or object underlying the written law`) THEN JUST `the second interpretation`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `Why material outside the written law is consulted` IS ONE OF
    `to confirm the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text, in its context and with its purpose`
    `to ascertain the meaning when the provision is ambiguous or obscure`
    `to ascertain the meaning when the ordinary meaning leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or unreasonable`

-- src:908 | (2) Subject to subsection (4), in the interpretation of a provision of a
-- src:909 | written law, if any material not forming part of the written law is
-- src:910 | capable of assisting in the ascertainment of the meaning of the
-- src:911 | provision, consideration may be given to that material —
-- src:913 | (a) to confirm that the meaning of the provision is the ordinary
-- src:914 | meaning conveyed by the text of the provision taking into
-- src:915 | account its context in the written law and the purpose or
-- src:916 | object underlying the written law; or
-- src:918 | (b) to ascertain the meaning of the provision when —
-- src:920 | (i) the provision is ambiguous or obscure; or
-- src:922 | (ii) the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the
-- src:923 | provision taking into account its context in the
-- src:924 | written law and the purpose or object underlying the
-- src:929 | written law leads to a result that is manifestly absurd
-- src:930 | or unreasonable.
@ref s 9A(2) (src:908-930)
GIVEN `material not forming part of the written law is capable of assisting in ascertaining the meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose of consulting it` IS A `Why material outside the written law is consulted`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`consideration may be given to the material` `material not forming part of the written law is capable of assisting in ascertaining the meaning` `the purpose of consulting it` MEANS
    IF `material not forming part of the written law is capable of assisting in ascertaining the meaning`
    THEN CONSIDER `the purpose of consulting it`
         WHEN `to confirm the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text, in its context and with its purpose` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `to ascertain the meaning when the provision is ambiguous or obscure` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `to ascertain the meaning when the ordinary meaning leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or unreasonable` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Material section 9A(3) names` IS ONE OF
    `matters in the document containing the text of the written law, as printed or published by the Government Printer`
    `an explanatory statement relating to the Bill`
    `the Minister's second reading speech`
    `relevant material in an official record of debates in Parliament`
    `a treaty or other international agreement referred to in the written law`
    `a document declared by the written law to be a relevant document`
    `any other material`

-- src:932 | (3) Without limiting subsection (2), the material that may be
-- src:933 | considered in accordance with that subsection in the interpretation of
-- src:934 | a provision of a written law includes —
-- src:936 | (a) all matters not forming part of the written law that are set
-- src:937 | out in the document containing the text of the written law
-- src:938 | as purporting to be printed or published by the Government
-- src:939 | Printer;
-- src:941 | [Act 5 of 2025 wef 09/03/2025]
-- src:943 | (b) any explanatory statement relating to the Bill containing
-- src:944 | the provision;
-- src:946 | (c) the speech made in Parliament by a Minister on the
-- src:947 | occasion of the moving by that Minister of a motion that
-- src:948 | the Bill containing the provision be read a second time in
-- src:949 | Parliament;
-- src:951 | (d) any relevant material in any official record of debates in
-- src:952 | Parliament;
-- src:954 | (e) any treaty or other international agreement that is referred
-- src:955 | to in the written law; and
-- src:957 | (f) any document that is declared by the written law to be a
-- src:958 | relevant document for the purposes of this section.
@ref s 9A(3) (src:932-958)
GIVEN `the material` IS A `Material section 9A(3) names`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 9A(3) names the material as material that may be considered` `the material` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the material`
    WHEN `any other material` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:960 | (4) In determining whether consideration should be given to any
-- src:961 | material in accordance with subsection (2), or in determining the
-- src:962 | weight to be given to any such material, regard must be had, in
-- src:963 | addition to any other relevant matters, to —
-- src:965 | (a) the desirability of persons being able to rely on the
-- src:966 | ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision
-- src:967 | taking into account its context in the written law and the
-- src:968 | purpose or object underlying the written law; and
-- src:970 | (b) the need to avoid prolonging legal or other proceedings
-- src:971 | without compensating advantage.
@ref s 9A(4) (src:960-971)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the matters to which regard must be had in deciding whether to consider material and what weight to give it` MEANS
    LIST "the desirability of persons being able to rely on the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision taking into account its context in the written law and the purpose or object underlying the written law", "the need to avoid prolonging legal or other proceedings without compensating advantage", "any other relevant matters"

§ `Section 9B -- Changes to style not to affect meaning`

-- src:978 | 9B. Where —
-- src:980 | (a) a provision of an Act has expressed an idea in a particular
-- src:981 | form of words; and
-- src:983 | (b) a revised edition or a later provision of that Act, or a later
-- src:984 | Act, appears to have expressed the same idea in a different
-- src:985 | form of words for the purpose of using a clearer style,
-- src:987 | the ideas are not to be taken to be different merely because different
-- src:988 | forms of words were used.
@ref s 9B (src:978-988)
GIVEN `a provision of an Act has expressed an idea in a particular form of words` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a later revised edition, provision or Act appears to express the same idea in different words, for a clearer style` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the ideas are taken to be different merely because the forms of words differ` `a provision of an Act has expressed an idea in a particular form of words` `a later revised edition, provision or Act appears to express the same idea in different words, for a clearer style` MEANS
    IF `a provision of an Act has expressed an idea in a particular form of words`
       AND `a later revised edition, provision or Act appears to express the same idea in different words, for a clearer style`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 11 to 14 -- repeal and its consequences for other written law`

-- src:1014 | 11. Where any Act or part of an Act is repealed, subsidiary
-- src:1015 | legislation issued under or made in virtue thereof remains in force so
-- src:1016 | far as it is not inconsistent with the repealing Act and unless the
-- src:1017 | contrary intention appears until it has been revoked or replaced by
-- src:1018 | subsidiary legislation issued or made under the provisions of the
-- src:1019 | repealing Act.
@ref s 11 (src:1014-1019)
GIVEN `the subsidiary legislation was issued under or in virtue of the repealed Act or part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is inconsistent with the repealing Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been revoked or replaced by subsidiary legislation under the repealing Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the subsidiary legislation remains in force after the Act or part is repealed` `the subsidiary legislation was issued under or in virtue of the repealed Act or part` `it is inconsistent with the repealing Act` `it has been revoked or replaced by subsidiary legislation under the repealing Act` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the subsidiary legislation was issued under or in virtue of the repealed Act or part`) OR `a contrary intention appears`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST ((NOT `it is inconsistent with the repealing Act`) AND (NOT `it has been revoked or replaced by subsidiary legislation under the repealing Act`))

-- src:1026 | 12. Where any written law repealing in whole or in part any former
-- src:1027 | written law is itself repealed, the last repeal does not revive the
-- src:1028 | written law or the provisions previously repealed, unless words are
-- src:1029 | added reviving that written law or those provisions.
@ref s 12 (src:1026-1029)
GIVEN `the repealing written law is itself repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `words are added reviving the former written law or provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the last repeal revives the written law or provisions previously repealed` `the repealing written law is itself repealed` `words are added reviving the former written law or provisions` MEANS
    IF `the repealing written law is itself repealed`
    THEN JUST `words are added reviving the former written law or provisions`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1033 | 13. Where any written law which has been amended by any other
-- src:1034 | written law is itself repealed, the repeal is deemed to include the
-- src:1035 | repeal of all written laws or parts of written laws by which the
-- src:1036 | firstmentioned written law has been amended.
@ref s 13 (src:1033-1036)
GIVEN `a written law that has been amended by another written law is repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other written law is one by which it was amended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the repeal is deemed to include the repeal of the amending written law` `a written law that has been amended by another written law is repealed` `the other written law is one by which it was amended` MEANS
    IF `a written law that has been amended by another written law is repealed` THEN JUST `the other written law is one by which it was amended` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1040 | 14. Where a written law repeals wholly or in part any former
-- src:1041 | written law and substitutes other provision therefor, the repealed
-- src:1042 | written law remains in force until the substituted provision comes into
-- src:1043 | operation.
@ref s 14 (src:1040-1043)
GIVEN `a written law repeals a former written law wholly or in part and substitutes other provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the substituted provision has come into operation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the repealed written law remains in force` `a written law repeals a former written law wholly or in part and substitutes other provision` `the substituted provision has come into operation` MEANS
    IF `a written law repeals a former written law wholly or in part and substitutes other provision` AND (NOT `the substituted provision has come into operation`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 15 -- References to amended and re-enacted provisions`

-- src:1047 | 15.—(1) Where in any written law a reference is made to another
-- src:1048 | written law, the reference is, except where the context otherwise
-- src:1049 | requires, deemed to include a reference to the last mentioned written
-- src:1050 | law as the same may from time to time be amended.
@ref s 15(1) (src:1047-1050)
GIVEN `a written law refers to another written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the reference includes the other written law as amended from time to time` `a written law refers to another written law` `the context otherwise requires` MEANS
    IF `a written law refers to another written law` AND (NOT `the context otherwise requires`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1052 | (2) Where any written law repeals and re-enacts, with or without
-- src:1053 | modification, any provision of a former written law, then, unless the
-- src:1054 | contrary intention appears —
-- src:1056 | (a) any reference in any other written law to the provision so
-- src:1057 | repealed is to be construed as a reference to the provision
-- src:1058 | so re‑enacted;
@ref s 15(2)(a) (src:1052-1058)
GIVEN `a written law repeals and re-enacts a provision of a former written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a reference to the provision repealed is construed as a reference to the provision re-enacted` `a written law repeals and re-enacts a provision of a former written law` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `a written law repeals and re-enacts a provision of a former written law` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1052 | (2) Where any written law repeals and re-enacts, with or without
-- src:1053 | modification, any provision of a former written law, then, unless the
-- src:1054 | contrary intention appears —
-- src:1060 | (b) insofar as any subsidiary legislation made or other thing
-- src:1061 | done under the provision so repealed, or having effect as if
-- src:1062 | so made or done, could have been made or done under the
-- src:1063 | provision so re‑enacted, it has effect as if made or done
-- src:1064 | under that provision.
@ref s 15(2)(b) (src:1052-1064)
GIVEN `a written law repeals and re-enacts a provision of a former written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it could have been made or done under the provision re-enacted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`subsidiary legislation made or a thing done under the provision repealed has effect as if made or done under the provision re-enacted` `a written law repeals and re-enacts a provision of a former written law` `it could have been made or done under the provision re-enacted` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `a written law repeals and re-enacts a provision of a former written law` AND `it could have been made or done under the provision re-enacted` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 16 -- Effect of repeal`

DECLARE `What a repeal might do` IS ONE OF
    `revive anything not in force or existing when the repeal takes effect`
    `affect the previous operation of the repealed law or anything duly done or suffered under it`
    `affect a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it`
    `affect a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred for an offence against it`
    `affect an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, liability or penalty`

-- src:1071 | 16.—(1) Where a written law repeals in whole or in part any other
-- src:1072 | written law, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the repeal
-- src:1073 | does not —
-- src:1075 | (a) revive anything not in force or existing at the time at which
-- src:1076 | the repeal takes effect;
-- src:1078 | (b) affect the previous operation of any written law so repealed
-- src:1079 | or anything duly done or suffered under any written law so
-- src:1080 | repealed;
-- src:1082 | (c) affect any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired,
-- src:1083 | accrued or incurred under any written law so repealed;
-- src:1085 | (d) affect any penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in
-- src:1086 | respect of any offence committed against any written law
-- src:1087 | so repealed; or
-- src:1089 | (e) affect any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in
-- src:1090 | respect of any such right, privilege, obligation, liability,
-- src:1091 | penalty, forfeiture or punishment as aforesaid; and any
-- src:1092 | such investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be
-- src:1093 | instituted, continued or enforced, and any such penalty,
-- src:1094 | forfeiture or punishment may be imposed, as if the
-- src:1095 | repealing law had not been passed.
@ref s 16(1) (src:1071-1095)
GIVEN `the repeal` IS A `What a repeal might do`
      `a written law repeals another in whole or in part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the repeal does this` `the repeal` `a written law repeals another in whole or in part` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `a written law repeals another in whole or in part` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`)
    THEN CONSIDER `the repeal`
         WHEN `revive anything not in force or existing when the repeal takes effect` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `affect the previous operation of the repealed law or anything duly done or suffered under it` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `affect a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `affect a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred for an offence against it` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `affect an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, liability or penalty` THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 16(1)(e) the proceeding, remedy or penalty may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing law had not been passed (src:1089-1095)
GIVEN `it is an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of a right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment under the repealed law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`it may be instituted, continued or enforced, or the penalty imposed, as if the repealing law had not been passed` `it is an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of a right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment under the repealed law` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `it is an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of a right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment under the repealed law` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `What counts as a repeal in section 16` IS ONE OF
    `a repeal effected by implication`
    `the abrogation or limitation of the effect of the written law or part`
    `the exclusion of the application of the written law or part to any person, subject matter or circumstance`
    `the expiry, lapse or other ceasing to have effect of the written law`
    `something else`

-- src:1097 | (2) A reference in this section to the repeal of a written law in whole
-- src:1098 | or in part includes a reference to —
-- src:1100 | (a) a repeal effected by implication;
-- src:1102 | (b) the abrogation or limitation of the effect of the written law
-- src:1103 | or part; and
-- src:1105 | (c) the exclusion of the application of the written law or part to
-- src:1106 | any person, subject matter or circumstance.
-- src:1108 | (3) Where a written law expires, lapses or otherwise ceases to have
-- src:1109 | effect, this section applies as if the written law had been repealed by
-- src:1110 | another written law.
@ref s 16(2), (3) (src:1097-1110)
GIVEN `the event` IS A `What counts as a repeal in section 16`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 16 treats the event as a repeal` `the event` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `A part of a written law` IS ONE OF
    `a provision`
    `words`
    `figures`
    `drawings`
    `symbols`
    `something else`

-- src:1115 | (4) A reference in this section to a part of a written law includes a
-- src:1116 | reference to any provision of, or words, figures, drawings or symbols
-- src:1117 | in, the written law.
@ref s 16(4) (src:1115-1117)
GIVEN `the part` IS A `A part of a written law`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is a part of a written law for section 16` `the part` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the part`
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Sections 17 and 18 -- amending Acts; expiry of a written law`

-- src:1121 | 17. Where an Act amends or adds to any Act, the amending Act is,
-- src:1122 | so far as is consistent with the tenor thereof, and unless the contrary
-- src:1123 | intention appears, to be construed as one with the amended Act and as
-- src:1124 | part thereof.
@ref s 17 (src:1121-1124)
GIVEN `an Act amends or adds to an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `construing it as one with the amended Act is consistent with its tenor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the amending Act is construed as one with the amended Act and as part of it` `an Act amends or adds to an Act` `construing it as one with the amended Act is consistent with its tenor` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `an Act amends or adds to an Act` AND `construing it as one with the amended Act is consistent with its tenor` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1128 | 18. The expiration of a written law does not affect any civil or
-- src:1129 | criminal proceeding previously commenced under the written law,
-- src:1130 | but every such proceeding may be continued and everything in
-- src:1131 | relation thereto may be done in all respects as if the written law
-- src:1132 | continued in force.
@ref s 18 (src:1128-1132)
GIVEN `a written law has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is civil or criminal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was commenced under the written law before the expiration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the proceeding may be continued as if the written law continued in force` `a written law has expired` `the proceeding is civil or criminal` `it was commenced under the written law before the expiration` MEANS
    IF `a written law has expired` AND `the proceeding is civil or criminal` AND `it was commenced under the written law before the expiration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
